        "t2": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<h2>Digestion — where the benefits start</h2><p>This is the most immediate and obvious benefit. A daily probiotic re-establishes the friendly bacteria that should naturally live in your gut but get wiped out by antibiotics, processed food, stress, and ageing. The result is less bloating, smoother bowel movements, reduced gas, relief from IBS symptoms, and better lactose tolerance.</p><p>Most users feel digestive improvements within 5-7 days of starting Velobiotics. By week two, the change is usually undeniable.</p><h2>Immunity — your hidden defence system</h2><p>About 70% of your immune cells live in your gut. They're trained, day in and day out, by the bacteria around them. A diverse microbiome trains a sharp immune system that distinguishes friend from foe. A depleted microbiome trains an immune system that either underreacts (frequent infections) or overreacts (allergies, autoimmunity).</p><p>Clinical studies consistently show probiotic supplementation reduces frequency and duration of respiratory and gastrointestinal infections — especially in children, the elderly, and people under chronic stress.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<h2>Mood, mental health, and the gut-brain axis</h2><p>The gut and brain are connected by the vagus nerve and a constant stream of biochemical signals. Up to 90% of your body's serotonin — the \"happiness neurotransmitter\" — is made in your gut, not your brain. Up to 50% of dopamine. Roughly half of GABA, the calming neurotransmitter.</p><p>Research now consistently shows that specific probiotic strains (especially <em>Lactobacillus helveticus</em> and <em>Bifidobacterium longum</em>) reduce symptoms of anxiety and depression. The mechanism: a healthier gut microbiome produces more of these mood-regulating neurotransmitters and reduces inflammatory signals that drive depressive symptoms.</p><h2>Weight, metabolism, and blood sugar</h2><p>Your microbiome influences how many calories you absorb from food, how your body stores fat, and how your insulin responds to meals. Specific strains (notably <em>Lactobacillus gasseri</em>) have been shown in randomised trials to reduce visceral fat and waist circumference. Others improve insulin sensitivity and blood sugar control. Probiotics are not a weight-loss drug, but they tilt the metabolic landscape in your favour.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t4": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<h2>Skin — the gut-skin axis</h2><p>Acne, eczema, rosacea, psoriasis — most chronic skin conditions are inflammatory at their root, and the inflammation often originates in a leaky, imbalanced gut. Probiotics seal the gut barrier, reduce systemic inflammation, and the skin responds.</p><p>Users typically see skin clarity improvements over 6-8 weeks of consistent use. Our Almasi range specifically targets skin, hair, and nail health by combining probiotics with collagen peptides and beauty nutrients.</p><h2>Women's health</h2><p>The vaginal microbiome is its own ecosystem, dominated by <em>Lactobacillus</em> strains that maintain healthy pH and prevent overgrowth of bacterial vaginosis and yeast. Antibiotics, hormonal contraceptives, stress, and sexual activity can disrupt it. Targeted oral probiotics (our Femina range) re-colonise the vaginal flora and dramatically reduce recurrent BV and yeast infections.</p><h2>The bottom line</h2><p>A daily probiotic is one of the highest-leverage supplements you can take. It supports six major body systems simultaneously, has an excellent safety profile, and the benefits compound over time. The catch is that delivery matters more than dosage — which is why Velobiotics builds its entire range around MEP encapsulation.</p>"
          }
